{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_boe_costing_portal", "label": "BOE Costing Portal", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L1-L8", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately self-contained: both services, all configuration, the database schema and a sample Bill of Entry live in one folder so nothing outside it is required to run the system."}, {"id": "readme_two_service_architecture", "label": "Two-Service Architecture (Python parser + TypeScript portal)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L92-L118", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The TypeScript portal cannot read a PDF. A separate Python process exists for exactly one action (PDF upload); rewriting the x-coordinate extractor in TypeScript would mean re-deriving every watermark, OCR and multi-invoice edge case. The two services are coupled by a single config line, NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL."}, {"id": "readme_boe_parser", "label": "boe_parser.py - ICEGATE PDF to structured data", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L18", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Called 'the crown jewel'; it is the sole reason a Python service exists at all."}, {"id": "readme_x_coordinate_extraction", "label": "X-Coordinate PDF Extraction with pdfplumber", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L94-L97", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Extracting by x-coordinate rather than by text flow is what makes the parser survive watermark bleed, OCR spelling variants and multi-invoice numbering."}, {"id": "readme_manual_entry_fallback", "label": "Manual Entry Bypasses the Backend", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L104-L109", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Manual entry writes straight to Supabase because it is the fallback for when parsing fails - it must not depend on the thing that failed."}, {"id": "readme_api_base_url", "label": "NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L111-L118", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The single seam between portal and parser; pointing it at localhost, Cloud Run or another machine requires no code change."}, {"id": "readme_supabase_persistence", "label": "Supabase Persistence and Key Split", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L41-L54", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Backend and frontend point at the same Supabase project but use different keys: the backend prefers service_role (it runs server-side and Storage uploads need it), the frontend must use anon because that key reaches the browser."}, {"id": "readme_costing_ts", "label": "costing.ts - the costing engine", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L26-L27", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Single source of truth for the maths; pinned down by 35 tests that need no database."}, {"id": "readme_costing_model", "label": "Landed Costing Model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L122-L140", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ported from the C-SHEET of the Excel template the team has always costed against, so portal output stays comparable with the historical spreadsheet."}, {"id": "readme_c_sheet_excel_template", "label": "C-SHEET Excel Template", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L123-L124", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_expense_pool_apportionment", "label": "Value-Proportional Expense Pool Apportionment", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L126-L138", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One expense pool split by declared-value share (Fi/sum F), so changing any expense moves every item's slice in proportion and changing an item's price recomputes the shares before the split."}, {"id": "readme_igst_exclusion", "label": "IGST Excluded from Cost", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L139-L140", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "IGST is a creditable input tax, so it is cash flow rather than cost; it is still reported separately as part of the cyber receipt."}, {"id": "readme_expanded_expense_pool", "label": "Expanded Expense Pool (departure from spreadsheet)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L144-L148", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The template's I9 = I8+I7+I6+I5 silently dropped Supplier Freight, Bank Charges and Own Bank Charges from cost per piece after displaying them in K6:K8. Including them makes portal figures read higher than the old spreadsheet wherever those are non-zero - that difference is the bug being fixed, not a regression."}, {"id": "readme_floating_duty", "label": "Fixed vs Floating Duty", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L150-L154", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A BOE records duty amounts, never rates, so effective rates are back-computed from what customs actually charged. Duty is held fixed by default and may float with value; switching mode with nothing else changed must not move any number, and that invariant is a test."}, {"id": "readme_scenarios", "label": "What-If Scenarios", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L156-L170", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every scenario input is nullable and means 'inherit the actual', so a new scenario reproduces the actual costing exactly until something is deliberately changed."}, {"id": "readme_foc_items", "label": "FOC Items Keep Declared Value in the Apportionment Base", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L161-L164", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Free-of-charge goods still ship and are still assessed, so keeping their declared value in the base stops freight shifting onto the paid items. A second toggle decides whether duty applies."}, {"id": "readme_duplicated_items", "label": "Duplicated Scenario Items Derive Duty from Source Rates", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L165-L167", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Duplicates always derive duty from their source's rates even when duty is fixed, because locking a copy to the source's actual amounts would charge the same customs payment twice."}, {"id": "readme_freight_mode", "label": "freight_mode is a Label Only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L168-L170", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Freight can be typed as a total or computed as rate x weight / volume / containers; the Air/Sea label changes no number, so it carries no arithmetic meaning."}, {"id": "readme_no_authentication", "label": "No Authentication (open RLS policies)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L176-L179", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "RLS is enabled with fully open policies so the portal works today; anyone with the anon key can read and write. IAP or Supabase Auth is required before this leaves the office."}, {"id": "readme_base_tables_reconstruction", "label": "sql/000_base_tables.sql is a Reconstruction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L180-L183", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Those tables were created by hand and their DDL was never checked in; column names were read back from the live database and types inferred from the code - good enough for a fresh environment but unverified for migrations."}, {"id": "readme_parser_bugs", "label": "Four Confirmed Parser Bugs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L184-L194", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_parse_scheme_g_bug", "label": "parse_scheme_g misreads quantity as BCD foregone", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L185-L188", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Part III row matches the column shape the function looks for. Harmless when cash BCD is non-zero, but on a licence-paid BOE it would write the wrong BCD."}, {"id": "readme_watermark_bleed_bug", "label": "ASSESSED COPY Watermark Bleeds into Descriptions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L189-L190", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The diagonal watermark injects stray letters into item descriptions (example: 'Super Charger 5AE')."}, {"id": "readme_page_footer_bug", "label": "Page Footers Appended to Last Description", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L191-L192", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Example artifact: 'Playmate 2 RemoSte Page 2 Of 7'."}, {"id": "readme_importer_name_missing", "label": "importer_name Never Extracted", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L193", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_margin_not_displayed", "label": "Margin Computed but Not Displayed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L194-L195", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "margin_pct drives sellingPerPiece / totalSelling, which nothing currently renders."}, {"id": "readme_no_excel_export", "label": "No Excel Export", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L196-L197", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The old Python Excel writer was deliberately not carried over so that costing.ts stays the single source of truth for the maths."}, {"id": "readme_scenarios_no_versioning", "label": "Scenarios Do Not Version", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L198", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Editing a scenario overwrites it; no history is kept."}, {"id": "readme_dev_scripts", "label": "dev.ps1 / dev.sh Service Launchers", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_boe_costing_portal", "target": "readme_two_service_architecture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L92-L118", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_two_service_architecture", "target": "readme_boe_parser", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_locatio